
=== A. Complex quantum theory: ELEM2 selects n <= 2; GEOM2 / SF2 hold at every n (the converse test) ===
NOTE [written] A.ELEM2_fails_n_ge_3  -- for pure x = |v><v|, y = |w><w| in M_n(C), m = (x+y)/2 has rank <= 2 < n; a kernel vector chi of m gives the state z = |chi><chi|/<chi|chi> with <chi|(m + eps(m - z))|chi> = -eps<chi|chi> < 0 for every eps > 0, so m is a boundary state.  Hence ELEM2 fails for every n >= 3 and every pair; checked exactly on the instances below.
NOTE [written] A.GEOM2_holds_all_n  -- genFace(D_n, m) = {states supported on K = span(v, w)}, dim K = 2; for an effect 0 <= E <= I and rho supported on K: tr(E rho) = 1 iff supp rho is in K cap ker(I - E).  dim(K cap ker(I-E)) is 0 or 1 (certain face empty or one pure state) or 2 (E identically 1 on the face, i.e. not proper on it).  So SF2 holds for every effect, every pair face, every n; and since a midpoint of two distinct states on a 2-dim space has rank 2 (full on K), every pair face is relatively strictly convex (GEOM2).  Checked exactly on the instances below.
